 all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, the service is healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions with an error rate of 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before deploying it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 14870, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_019S9U8RFLJz1BDtQFWwMR1q", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 14870, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019S9U8RFLJz1BDtQFWwMR1q", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18797, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's now passing health checks. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** I picked v2.3.0 because it's the most recent release that was healthy in production. It now runs in all three regions, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failed v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback to v2.3.0 and the recovery. It also says v2.3.1 shouldn't be deployed again until the cause is found.\n\nThe test build of this release, v2.3.1-rc, was already marked unhealthy in staging before v2.3.1 went to production. It's worth finding out why it was promoted anyway.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017dfZABxNTWWoAdyEVCNiqF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, 