dent INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** I picked v2.3.0 because it's the most recent release that was healthy in production. It now runs in all three regions, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failed v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback to v2.3.0 and the recovery. It also says v2.3.1 shouldn't be deployed again until the cause is found.\n\nThe test build of this release, v2.3.1-rc, was already marked unhealthy in staging before v2.3.1 went to production. It's worth finding out why it was promoted anyway.", "type": "text"}]}]}